  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Symbiose Academy is Kevin and Anissa, dog trainers based in La Cadière-d'Azur. Their approach aims for a dog that is "stable, reliable and comfortable in its own skin": recall, loose-lead walking, impulse control and reactivity management, with work adapted to powerful or sensitive dogs. Sessions take place in the field, at home or by video, and a dog club offers group sessions, workshops and educational walks. They also make made-to-measure gear (leads, long lines, harnesses, muzzles).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Appointments are made Monday to Saturday, 9am to 8pm, via the website; they work in the Var and the Bouches-du-Rhône, at home depending on the area. The site describes two strands: "balanced" training based on understanding the dog, consistency and emotional stability, and a behaviour and rehabilitation strand when problems are already established (reactivity, fears, aggression, anxiety, over-excitement). It reminds visitors that any medical problem is a matter for the vet. The Izanagi dog club, presented on the same site, is for dogs in training, reactive or sensitive dogs, powerful or atypical dogs; the Izanagi shop sells handmade gear (leads, long lines, collars, harnesses, muzzles) made to the dog's build.</p>
      <p>This listing was first classed under dog sitting, but the current official website does not mention boarding. It does not publish the prices of the training packages either.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: for a dog that is reactive or difficult on walks, ask for a first session in a real situation (in town or in nature) rather than in a training field; this is what their method emphasises.</div>
      <div class="callout">Check before booking: if you are looking for somewhere to leave your dog, ask whether boarding is offered, as the official website does not mention it; package prices are to be requested.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Bandol vineyards and the coves along the coast between Sanary-sur-Mer and La Ciotat are accessible from La Cadière d'Azur.</p>
